# HL-BOS environment variables -- EXAMPLE ONLY. Placeholders, never real values.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; keep it that way.
#
# The authoritative definition of these variables is ENV_SPEC in
# packages/config/src/env.ts. That is what validates them at startup, and it
# is what this file documents. If the two disagree, env.ts wins.
#
# CLASSIFICATION -- read before adding anything here:
#
#   browser-safe    Inlined into the client bundle. Assume the entire world
#                   can read it. MUST be NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefixed.
#   server-only     Server runtime only. NEVER NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefixed.
#   ci-only         CI only. Never present at application runtime.
#   supabase-secret Supabase secret / Vault entry. Read by Edge Functions.
#   provider-secret Third-party credential. Server-only, and additionally
#                   accessed only through its provider abstraction.
#
# Rule, enforced by CI (scripts/check-no-public-secrets.sh) and by ESLint:
# never put a private secret behind NEXT_PUBLIC_. It is public the moment it
# builds.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime  [server-only]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which HL-BOS deployment environment this process belongs to.
# Distinct from NODE_ENV: a preview deploy is NODE_ENV=production but
# HL_BOS_ENV=preview.
# One of: local | preview | staging | production
HL_BOS_ENV=local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase  [browser-safe]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Project URL. Genuinely public -- it is in every client request.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Publishable (anon) key. Browser-visible by design.
# This key is NOT a security boundary -- Row Level Security is. Anything
# reachable with this key is reachable by the public internet.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase  [server-only]  ***  BYPASSES ALL ROW LEVEL SECURITY  ***
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Service-role key. Server-only, always.
# Never import into a client component. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC.
# If this reaches a browser bundle, every tenant's data is readable by every
# visitor. Treat a leak as a full credential rotation event.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT YET REQUIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe, Twilio, Anthropic/OpenAI/Gemini and email provider credentials are
# deliberately absent. They are added by the phase that introduces the
# capability needing them (Phases 3 and 4). Listing them now would force
# operators to populate variables that nothing reads.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ATS Resume Optimizer  [server-only, all optional]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read by apps/ats-resume-optimizer/src/lib/config.ts, NOT by ENV_SPEC. That
# app is single-operator and local, with no Supabase dependency, so it owns its
# own env boundary in one file rather than joining the platform contract. If it
# later gains Supabase Auth, these move into ENV_SPEC and this note goes away.
#
# Every variable here is optional: with none of them set, the app runs, seeds a
# labelled sample profile, and every feature works on the built-in rules engine.

# Anthropic API key. Enables Claude for two jobs only -- re-reading a job
# posting, and proposing bullet phrasing. Whatever it proposes is re-checked
# against the candidate's own evidence before it can reach a resume.
# Server-only. Never NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Which model, when a key is set.
# ATS_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Where the local JSON store is written. Relative paths resolve against the
# app directory. This file holds a real person's career history -- put it
# somewhere backed up, and somewhere other people cannot read.
# ATS_DATA_DIR=.data

# Set to false to start with an empty workspace instead of the sample profile.
# ATS_SEED_DEMO=true

# --- Deployment (Coolify) -------------------------------------------------
#
# The app decides for itself whether a sign-in is required, from HL_BOS_ENV
# plus whether Supabase is configured. It has three modes:
#
#   local          not deployed, no provider -> no sign-in, file store
#   authenticated  provider configured       -> sign-in required
#   refuse         deployed, no provider     -> serves nothing but an
#                                               explanation page
#
# The last one is deliberate: forgetting one variable must not be the
# difference between a private career database and a public one. Deploying
# therefore needs BOTH NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values (already documented
# above, under Supabase) set as BUILD variables, because Next inlines them
# into the browser bundle at build time.
#
# See apps/ats-resume-optimizer/DEPLOYMENT.md.
